          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $m_0=1$ and $m_n=z^n+z^{-n}$ for $n\\ge1$ be the A1 Weyl orbit sums. The degree of a nonzero Laurent polynomial $\\sum_k a_kz^k$ is $\\max\\{|k|:a_k\\ne0\\}$. For every $n\\ge0$, the operator $\\mathcal D$ of [[def-daha-a1-symmetric-macdonald-operator]] sends $m_n$ to\n\n$$\n\\mathcal Dm_n=\\lambda_nm_n+\\sum_{0\\le j<n}d_{n,j}m_j,\\qquad \\lambda_n=tq^n+t^{-1}q^{-n},\n$$\n\nwith coefficients $d_{n,j}\\in K$. In particular, $\\mathcal D$ preserves the symmetric Laurent-polynomial space.",
