        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "def-daha-a1-double-affine-hecke-algebra",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Use the rank-one root datum, affine actions, field $K$, and Laurent polynomials $B_{i,m}$ from [[def-daha-a1-root-datum-and-parameter-conventions]] and [[lem-daha-a1-bernstein-quotients-are-laurent]]. Let $F$ be the free associative unital $K$-algebra on $Z,Z^{-1},T_0,T_1,\\pi$. Define the equal-parameter double-affine Hecke algebra\n\n$$\n\\mathcal H_{q,t}(A_1)=F/I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the two-sided ideal generated by the following relations:\n\n1. $ZZ^{-1}=Z^{-1}Z=1$.\n2. $\\pi^2=1$ and $\\pi T_0\\pi=T_1$ (hence also $\\pi T_1\\pi=T_0$).\n3. $(T_i-t)(T_i+t^{-1})=0$ for $i=0,1$.\n4. For every $m\\in\\mathbb Z$ and $i\\in\\{0,1\\}$,\n$$\nT_i Z^m-s_i(Z^m)T_i=(t-t^{-1})B_{i,m}(Z),\n$$\nwhere $s_1(Z^m)=Z^{-m}$ and $s_0(Z^m)=q^{-2m}Z^{-m}$.\n5. $\\pi Z\\pi=q^{-1}Z^{-1}$.\n\nThis is the rank-one root-datum DAHA presentation: $T_0,T_1$ are the affine Hecke generators, $Z$ is the weight-lattice generator, and $\\pi$ is the length-zero symmetry. There is no finite braid relation between $T_0$ and $T_1$ because the affine $A_1$ Coxeter label is infinite. The scalar normalization is $(T_i-t)(T_i+t^{-1})=0$; $q$ controls translations and is independent of $t$. The quotient is a definition, not a claim about a PBW basis or a faithful polynomial representation.\n\nThe fundamental translation is $y=\\pi s_1$, acting by the $q$-shift $z\\mapsto qz$; its DAHA lift is $Y=\\pi T_1$. The quadratic relation makes $T_1$ invertible, with $T_1^{-1}=T_1-(t-t^{-1})$.",
